//
// Conduit (--use-conduit) end-to-end run for the canon
// refuse-to-collapse-on-await predicate (`chainHasAwait` in
// CanonicalizeChannelPutsUtils.{h,cpp}, landed 2026-05-03 in this
// commit) — the puts-side variant.  Companion to:
//   test/Dialect/Conduit/conduit_canon_no_collapse_on_token_true.mlir
//     (lit-only at-site pin for the predicate)
//   test/npu-xrt/conduit_canon_no_collapse_on_link/conduit.lit
//     (link-refusal HW smoke; structural sibling, different predicate)
//   test/npu-xrt/conduit_canon_no_collapse_on_gets_with_await/conduit.lit
//     (gets-side counterpart of THIS smoke)
//
// Validates that canon's HomogeneousRepeatPattern (and
// ArithProgressionPattern, symmetric) does NOT collapse 4 structurally-
// identical IRON puts on a NON-LINKED shim-MM2S → compute channel when
// each put carries `aiex.dma_await_task` (per-issue ack) +
// `aiex.dma_free_task` (release marker) — chain shape `[true, false]`
// after dma-task-to-conduit lowering.
//
// Pre-fix, collapse → 1 configure × dma_repeat = 3 with the per-issue
// ack request inherited onto the merged single configure → firmware
// fires the BD 4 times back-to-back without per-chunk consumer ack
// pacing → HW stalls (XRT timeout).  Same root-cause class as the
// canon link-refusal landed in commit 375b0e5233.
//
// Post-fix, canon refuses on `chainHasAwait(refShape)`; Pass C emits
// 4 separate paced shim configures (each with its own per-issue ack);
// HW dispatch completes and the per-byte output check below passes.
//
// Pipeline: bare `--use-conduit` (no fusion flags — this test exercises
// canon refusal, not fusion).  aiecc.cpp:1492-1508 expands `--use-conduit`
// to `objectfifo-to-conduit, dma-task-to-conduit, conduit-canonicalize-
// channel-puts, conduit-depth-promote, conduit-to-dma`.
//
// PASS expectation: dispatch completes and output bytes match the
// spec-derived reference computed in test.cpp.  Hang/timeout would
// indicate the canon refusal regressed; wrong-bytes would indicate
// the chainHasAwait emit shape changed in a non-byte-equivalent way.
//
// REQUIRES: ryzen_ai, peano
//
// Kernel compute is inline bf16 load/store (the in-core scf.for copy
// loop in aie.mlir); Peano is required because xchesscc cannot select
// bf16 ops for an inline core (sibling pattern: `loadpdi/run.lit`,
// `vec_vec_add_objfifo_init/aie2.py`, `conduit_join_last_slice_overflow/
// conduit.lit`, `conduit_canon_no_collapse_on_link/conduit.lit`).  Use
// `--no-xchesscc --no-xbridge` to route the kernel compile through Peano.
//
// =============================================================================
// XFAIL — pinned 2026-05-03.  Surfaces a real LATENT Pass C emit bug exposed
// by (NOT caused by) the canon `chainHasAwait` refusal landed this commit.
// =============================================================================
//
// What this fixture pins (the canon refusal + smoke-fix-v2 design): with
// `chainHasAwait` refusal active, canon correctly leaves 4 separate paced
// MM2S configures on @in instead of collapsing them to 1 + dma_repeat=3.
// That's the SMOKE FIX V2 contract and it IS verified at the lit level by
// `test/Dialect/Conduit/conduit_canon_no_collapse_on_token_true.mlir`.
//
// Why this HW smoke XFAILs against current HEAD: Pass C's emit for the
// downstream tile S2MM consumer-side BD chain becomes NON-CIRCULAR when
// canon leaves N>depth separate paced configures (the post-refusal shape).
// Pre-refusal (canon collapses to 1 configure × dma_repeat), the BD chain
// emits correctly as a circular ring; post-refusal, the chain wraps to a
// dead-end last BD and the dispatch never returns a completion token →
// XRT timeout.  This is a real Pass C bug (NON-circular chain on the
// post-refusal emit shape), distinct from the canon predicate itself.
//
// Diagnostic provenance (verdict from puts-with-await-investigator,
// 2026-05-03 — Hypothesis B confirmed): captured artifacts at
//   /tmp/puts-with-await-capture/   (THIS fixture — failing IR)
//   /tmp/gets-with-await-capture/   (sibling gets-side fixture — passing IR;
//                                    its consumer-side BD chain stays
//                                    circular because gets sit on a different
//                                    Pass C emit branch than puts)
// IR diff between the two is the smoking gun: only the consumer-side tile
// BD-chain `next_bd` topology differs.  Canon's predicate is byte-identical
// in both; the divergence is downstream in Pass C.
//
// Why XFAIL (not delete): this fixture continues to validate the smoke fix v2
// design (canon refusal at the IR level — verified end-to-end by aiecc
// completing without canon-mode crashes on the post-refusal shape) AND it
// pins the latent Pass C bug for the eventual fixer.  Flips to PASS when the
// Pass C non-circular-chain bug on N>depth paced shim-MM2S → memtile-S2MM
// emit is fixed.  Tracked in CLAUDE.md "Active Open Bugs" (row added in
// task #57).
//
// Companion gets-side smoke (`conduit_canon_no_collapse_on_gets_with_await/`)
// is NOT XFAIL'd — it independently verifies canon refusal on the gets path
// AND happens to dodge the Pass C bug by virtue of a different downstream
// emit shape.  Together the two fixtures bracket the surface: gets-side
// proves the predicate works end-to-end; puts-side pins the residual Pass
// C bug that the predicate exposes.
//
// XFAIL: *
//
// RUN: cp %S/aie.mlir aie_arch.mlir
// RUN: %run_on_npu1% sed 's/NPUDEVICE/npu1_1col/g' -i aie_arch.mlir
// RUN: %run_on_npu2% sed 's/NPUDEVICE/npu2_1col/g' -i aie_arch.mlir
// RUN: %python aiecc.py --no-aiesim --no-xchesscc --no-xbridge --aie-generate-xclbin --aie-generate-npu-insts --no-compile-host --use-conduit --xclbin-name=aie.xclbin --npu-insts-name=insts.bin aie_arch.mlir
// RUN: clang %S/test.cpp -o test.exe -std=c++17 -Wall %xrt_flags -lrt -lstdc++ %test_utils_flags
// RUN: %run_on_npu1% ./test.exe -x aie.xclbin -k MLIR_AIE -i insts.bin
// RUN: %run_on_npu2% ./test.exe -x aie.xclbin -k MLIR_AIE -i insts.bin
